// ANIMDEFS.example — rename to "ANIMDEFS" (no extension) to activate.
//
// ZDoom-format data-driven texture/flat animation for TwoPointFive. This
// engine's parser (engine/animdefs) is clean-room from the format
// description; it understands `flat` / `texture` animation blocks and the
// `warp` / `warp2` swimming effect. `switch`, `cameratexture` and
// `animateddoor` are recognised only well enough to skip (they log a
// warning). An ANIMDEFS entry for a texture overrides the built-in / BOOM
// ANIMATED animation for that same name.
//
// Both renderers honour these: the software rasteriser and the Vulkan
// GPU-geometry path resolve textures by name, and the engine rewrites the
// live name each tic. `warp` is baked into a 32-phase frame cycle at level
// load (so it costs 32x the texture's size in RAM per warped texture).

// --- explicit frame list, per-frame durations -------------------------
// A slower, hand-timed nukage cycle (vanilla runs all four frames at 8).
flat NUKAGE1
    pic NUKAGE1 tics 10
    pic NUKAGE2 tics 6
    pic NUKAGE3 tics 10
    pic NUKAGE2 tics 6

// Numeric `pic N` — N is a 1-based offset from the base name's number, so
// this is BLOOD1, BLOOD2, BLOOD3 with a touch of duration jitter.
flat BLOOD1
    pic 1 tics 8
    pic 2 rand 6 12
    pic 3 tics 8

// `oscillate` plays the list forward then back (no repeated endpoints).
texture FIREMAG1
    pic FIREMAG1 tics 4
    pic FIREMAG2 tics 4
    pic FIREMAG3 tics 4
    oscillate

// Short `range` form: animate FIREBLU1..FIREBLU2 at 6 tics/frame.
texture FIREBLU1 range FIREBLU2 tics 6

// --- warp (swimming texture) -----------------------------------------
// `warp` = the classic small sine swim; `warp2` = a wider, rounder
// displacement. An optional trailing number scales the speed (1.0 = the
// engine's gentle default; higher is faster).
warp  flat    FWATER1
warp  flat    LAVA1        1.5
warp2 texture BFALL1
